   "text": "In this Act,\n“accompany” means for a person to maintain sufficient proximity to the person being accompanied to be able\n(a) to observe the person and communicate to that person by unamplified voice,\n(b) to directly supervise and provide instruction to that person and to ensure his or her safety, and\n(c) to exercise reasonable control over the person in order to ensure that the person acts in compliance with this Act while hunting; « accompagner »\n“Act” includes regulations made under this Act; « loi »\n“big game animal” means a member of a species of wildlife prescribed by the regulations as a species of big game animal; « gros gibier »\n“big game guiding permit” means a permit issued under subsection 58(1), and includes any conditions imposed on the permit; « permis de guide pour gros gibier »\n“Canadian citizen” has the same meaning as in the Citizenship Act (Canada);« citoyen canadien »\n“Concession and Compensation Review Board” means the Concession and Compensation Review Board established under subsection 192(2); « Conseil de révision des concessions et de l'indemnisation »\n“dwelling house” has the same meaning as in the Criminal Code (Canada); « maison d'habitation »\n“firearm” includes any device that propels a projectile by means of an explosion, compressed gas, springs or strings and, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, includes a rifle, shotgun, handgun, spring gun, longbow or crossbow; « arme à feu »\n“fur bearing animal” means a member of a species of wildlife prescribed by the regulations as a species of fur bearing animal; « animal à fourrure »\n“game bird” means a member of a species of wildlife prescribed by the regulations as a species of game bird; « gibier à plume »\n“game farm animal” means a member of a species of wildlife prescribed by the regulations as a species of game farm animal; « gibier d'une ferme d'élevage »\n“guide” means a person issued a licence under this Act authorizing the person to act as a guide, but does not include a special guide; « guide »\n“habitat” means the soil, water, food , vegetation and other components of the natural environment that are necessary to sustain wildlife; « habitat »\n“harass” includes worry, exhaust, fatigue, annoy, plague, pester, tease or torment, but does not include the lawful hunting, trapping, or capturing of wildlife; « harceler »\n“hunt” includes to shoot at, attract, search for, chase, flush, pursue, follow after or on the trail of, stalk or lie in wait for wildlife, or to attempt to do any of those things, whether or not wildlife is then or subsequently wounded, killed or captured,\n(a) with the intention to wound, kill or capture wildlife; or\n(b) while in the possession of a firearm or other weapon,\nexcept that “hunt” does not include trap; « chasser »\n“Inuvialuit” means those people known as Inuvialuit, Inuit or Eskimo who are beneficiaries under the Inuvialuit Final Agreement; « Inuvialuit »\n“Inuvialuit Final Agreement” means the land claims agreement between the Committee for Original Peoples’ Entitlement, representing the Inuvialuit of the Inuvialuit Settlement Region, and the Government of Canada, dated June 5, 1984, and includes amendments to that agreement dated December 14, 1987; « Convention définitive des Inuvialuit »\n“Inuvialuk” means an individual member of the Inuvialuit; « Inuvialuk »\n“licence” means a licence issued under this Act, and includes any conditions imposed on a licence; « licence »\n“Minister” means the Executive Council member responsible for the administration of this Act; « ministre »\n“non-resident” means a person who is not a Yukon resident; « non-résident »\n“operating certificate” means an operating certificate issued for an outfitting concession under subsection 54(1) and includes any conditions imposed on an operating certificate; « certificat d’exploitation »\n“outfitter” means an individual who holds an outfitting concession under this Act; « pourvoyeur »\n“outfitting concession” means an outfitting concession issued under Part 2 of this Act and includes any conditions imposed on an outfitting concession; « concession de pourvoirie »\n“outfitting concession area” means a geographic area prescribed by the regulations to be an outfitting concession area; « zone reliée à une concession de pourvoirie »\n“permanent resident” has the same meaning as in the Immigration Act (Canada); « résident permanent »\n“permit” means a permit issued under this Act and includes any conditions imposed on a permit; « permis »\n“private land” means land in respect of which a certificate of title has been issued under the Land Titles Act, 2015 and includes land held under a residential, industrial, commercial, agricultural or recreational lease from the Crown; « terrain privé »\n“small game animal” means a member of a species of wildlife prescribed by the regulations as a species of small game animal; « petit gibier »\n“specially protected wildlife” means any population, species or type of wildlife prescribed by the regulations as specially protected wildlife; « espèce faunique spécialement protégée »\n“traffic” means to buy, sell, trade or distribute for gain or consideration, or to offer to do so; « trafiquer »\n“trap” means\n(a) a device or contrivance used or designed to be used for capturing, injuring or killing wildlife, and includes a device or contrivance prescribed by the regulations to be a trap, but does not include a firearm; « piège »\n(b) using a device or contrivance referred to in paragraph (a) to capture, injure, or kill wildlife or to attempt to capture, injure, or kill wildlife; « piéger »\n“trapping concession” means a trapping concession issued under Part 2 of this Act and includes any conditions imposed on a trapping concession; « concession de piégeage »\n“trapping concession area” means a geographic area prescribed by the regulations to be a trapping concession area; « zone reliée à une concession de piégeage »\n“type” includes age, sex, conformation and phenotype; « type »\n“vehicle” includes an aircraft and any trailer or other contrivance drawn by a vehicle, but does not include a boat, unless the boat is on a trailer or other contrivance drawn by a vehicle; « véhicule »\n“wildlife” means a vertebrate animal of any species or type that is wild by nature, and includes wildlife in captivity, but does not include fish, wildlife in relation to which a permit has been issued under the Animal Protection and Control Act or a species of animal prescribed by the regulations not to be wildlife; « faune »\n“wildlife sanctuary” means an area prescribed by the regulations to be a wildlife sanctuary; « refuge faunique »\n“Yukon North Slope” means all those lands within the geographic limits of the Yukon Territory north of the height of land dividing the watersheds of the Porcupine River and the Beaufort Sea, and includes islands within twenty statute miles from the shores of the Beaufort Sea. « versant nord du Yukon »\n“Yukon resident” means\n(a) a person who is a Canadian citizen or permanent resident whose principal residence has been in the Yukon for a period of at least 12 months immediately prior to the time the person’s residence becomes material under this Act; and\n(b) who has been physically present in the Yukon for at least 185 days during the 12 month period described in paragraph (a); or\n(c) a person who belongs to a class of persons considered to be Yukon residents by the regulations. « résident du Yukon »",
   "part": "Interpretation",
   "heading": "Definitions",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s2",
   "number": "2",
   "text": "A reference in this Act to wildlife, or to any word or expression that includes wildlife, includes a reference to\n(a) the wildlife, whether dead or alive;\n(b) the whole or any part of the wildlife;\n(c) the wildlife at any stage of its development, unless it is inside the body of its parent; and\n(d) its gamete.",
   "part": "Interpretation",
   "heading": "Reference to wildlife",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s3",
   "number": "3",
   "text": "Where a period of time is expressed under this Act to be a period from one day to another, the period shall be reckoned inclusively of both the first and last day.",
   "part": "Interpretation",
   "heading": "Periods of time",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s4",
   "number": "4",
   "text": "A reference in this Act to a species includes a reference to any subspecies of that species and to any other lower taxonomic classification.",
   "part": "Interpretation",
   "heading": "Reference to species",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s5",
   "number": "5",
   "text": "For the purposes of this Act, the offspring that results from the natural or artificial breeding of wildlife shall be considered to belong to the species or subspecies of the parent that receives the most protection under this Act.",
   "part": "Interpretation",
   "heading": "Offspring of wildlife",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s6",
   "number": "6",
   "text": "No person shall hunt or trap a species or type of wildlife at any time in any area of the Yukon unless the hunting or trapping by that person of that species or type of wildlife at that time in that area is permitted under this Act.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "General prohibition",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s7",
   "number": "7",
   "text": "(1) Except under the authority of a licence or a permit, a person shall not hunt or trap\n(a) a big game animal;\n(b) a small game animal;\n(c) a game bird; or\n(d) a fur bearing animal.\n(2) Despite subsection (1), a person may, without a licence or a permit\n(a) hunt or trap a species of wildlife in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations; or\n(b) kill wildlife in the circumstances set out in sections 85, 86, and 87.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Requirement for hunting or trapping licence",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s8",
   "number": "8",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not hunt or trap specially protected wildlife.\n(2) A person shall not possess specially protected wildlife.\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to an Inuvialuk who hunts or traps specially protected wildlife in accordance with an allocation under section 207.\n(4) Subsection (2) does not apply to a person issued a permit in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Specially protected wildlife",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s9",
   "number": "9",
   "text": "(1) A person under 12 years of age shall not hunt a big game animal and a parent or guardian of a child under 12 years of age shall not permit the child to hunt a big game animal.\n(2) A person who is at least 12 years of age but not yet 16 years of age shall not hunt a big game animal except in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.\n(3) No person who is the parent or guardian of a child under 16 years of age shall permit the child to hunt any species or type of wildlife unless the child is accompanied by a person 19 years of age or older who is\n(a) the holder of a valid licence to hunt of a type that may be issued only to a Yukon resident; or\n(b) a guide provided by an outfitter in accordance with this Act.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Hunting by children",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s10",
   "number": "10",
   "text": "(1) A person who is in possession of a firearm for the purpose of hunting or trapping shall not discharge or handle the firearm, or cause it to be discharged or handled, without due care and attention or without reasonable consideration of people or property.\n(2) A person shall be considered to have acted without due care and attention or without reasonable consideration of people or property under subsection (1) if the person\n(a) hunts with a firearm that is in an unsafe condition;\n(b) hunts while his or her ability to do so is impaired by alcohol or a drug;\n(c) discharges a firearm in the dark;\n(d) discharges a firearm, or causes a projectile from a firearm to pass, on or across the travelled portion of a road that is normally used by the public, whether or not the safety of any person actually is endangered; or\n(e) discharges a firearm within one kilometre of a building which is a residence, whether or not the occupants are present in the building at the time the firearm is discharged, unless the person has the permission of the occupants to do so.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Careless use of firearm",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s11",
   "number": "11",
   "text": "A person shall not use a firearm to hunt wildlife in a manner designed to permit the firearm to discharge when it is not being physically held by the person.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Set firearms",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s12",
   "number": "12",
   "text": "A person shall not hunt or trap in a manner that causes or is likely to cause injury to a person, a domestic animal or livestock, or damage to crops or other personal property.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Injury to persons and damage to property",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s13",
   "number": "13",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not hunt or trap wildlife within one kilometre of a building which is a residence, whether or not the occupants are present in the building at the time, unless the person has the permission of the occupants to do so.\n(2) In a prosecution under subsection (1), the onus is on the accused to prove that he or she had the permission of the occupants to hunt or trap within one kilometre of the residence.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Hunting near a residence",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s14",
   "number": "14",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not carry a loaded firearm in or on a vehicle.\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a cartridge-loading firearm shall be considered to be loaded when a live shell or cartridge is in the breech or chamber of the firearm, and a muzzle-loading firearm shall be considered to be loaded when gun powder and a projectile are in the chamber of the firearm and an ignition device is in place on the firearm.\n(3) A person shall not discharge a firearm from a vehicle.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Firearms in vehicles",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s15",
   "number": "15",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not within any period of time capture or kill a greater number of wildlife of a particular species or type than is permitted under this Act for that period of time for that species or type.\n(2) A person shall not hunt or trap wildlife of a particular species or type after the person has captured or killed the maximum number of wildlife of that species or type that he or she is permitted under this Act to capture or kill in that period of time.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Bag limits",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s16",
   "number": "16",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not employ or offer to employ another person to kill or capture wildlife, or to take any egg or nest of a bird that is wild by nature.\n(2) A person shall not enter into or offer to enter into a contract with another person to kill or capture wildlife, or to take any egg or nest of a bird that is wild by nature.\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Employment of hunters",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s17",
   "number": "17",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not destroy, take or possess any egg or nest of a bird that belongs to a species that is wild by nature.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a person issued a permit in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.\n(3) This section does not apply to eggs or nests that are subject to the Migratory Birds Convention Act, 1994 (Canada).",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Nests and eggs",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s18",
   "number": "18",
   "text": "(1) No person shall have in his or her possession any decoy, appliance or material of any kind commonly used for the live capture of birds that are wild by nature.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a person issued a permit in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Possession of decoys to capture birds",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s19",
   "number": "19",
   "text": "A person shall not hunt or trap any species or type of wildlife otherwise than by the use of such firearms, traps or other devices as are\n(a) authorized for use by the conditions of the person’s licence for the killing or capturing of that species or type of wildlife; or\n(b) prescribed by the regulations for the killing or capturing of that species or type of wildlife if the person’s licence does not specify the firearms, traps or other devices which may be used.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Permitted weapons",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s20",
   "number": "20",
   "text": "A person shall not use a vehicle to chase, drive, flush, exhaust or fatigue wildlife for the purpose of hunting or to assist another person hunting.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Use of vehicles",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s21",
   "number": "21",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not use bait for hunting wildlife.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Use of bait",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s22",
   "number": "22",
   "text": "A person shall not use lighting or reflecting equipment for the purpose of hunting wildlife.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Use of lights",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s23",
   "number": "23",
   "text": "(1) In respect of any place where the sun rises and sets daily, a person shall not hunt wildlife during the period one hour after sunset to one hour before sunrise.\n(2) In respect of any place where the sun does not rise or set daily, a person shall not hunt wildlife during the period the centre of the sun’s disc is more than six degrees below the horizon.\n(3) The regulations may, for any area or part of the Yukon, prescribe the time of day deemed to be\n(a) sunset or sunrise for the purposes of subsection(1); or\n(b) the period when the sun’s disc is more than 6 degrees below the horizon for the purposes of subsection(2).",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "No hunting between sunset and sunrise",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s24",
   "number": "24",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not hunt wildlife from or by means of an aircraft.\n(2) A person shall be deemed to be hunting wildlife by means of an aircraft if he or she\n(a) hunts wildlife within 48 hours after locating it from an aircraft;\n(b) hunts wildlife within 48 hours after the wildlife is located from an aircraft by another person who communicates, directly or indirectly, information about its location or approximate location to the person hunting; or\n(c) locates wildlife from an aircraft and communicates, directly or indirectly, information about its location or approximate location to another person who hunts the wildlife within 48 hours of it being so located.\n(d) [Repealed S.Y. 2009, c.9, s.11]\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to a person issued a permit in the circumstances prescribed in the regulations to use an aircraft to hunt wildlife in order to conduct wildlife studies or research or for wildlife management purposes.\n(4) A person shall not hunt a big game animal within six hours of disembarking from an aircraft other than an aircraft operated by a commercial airline company on a regularly scheduled flight from one airport to another.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Use of aircraft",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s25",
   "number": "25",
   "text": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), a person shall not use a helicopter\n(a) to be transported, or to transport another person, to any place for the purpose of hunting a big game animal;\n(b) to be transported from a location or area where he or she has been on a hunting expedition for a big game animal, whether or not a big game animal has been taken;\n(c) to transport a person described in paragraph (b); or\n(d) to transport any part of a big game animal.\n(2) A conservation officer may, in writing, authorize the use of a helicopter if\n(a) a person requires emergency medical attention and it is not practicable to obtain such medical attention without the use of a helicopter;\n(b) there are other exigent circumstances which, in the opinion of the officer, warrant the use of a helicopter; or\n(c) the hunting or transport of a big game animal will be incidental to the lawful trapping activities of a person licensed to trap under this Act, and, in the opinion of the officer, it is not practicable to transport the person or big game animal without the use of a helicopter.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Use of helicopter",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s26",
   "number": "26",
   "text": "A person shall not transport any vehicle by helicopter for the purpose of hunting.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Transport vehicle by helicopter",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s27",
   "number": "27",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not use poison or drugs to kill, injure, disable or capture wildlife.\n(2) A person shall deemed to use poison or drugs to kill, injure, disable, or capture wildlife if the person\n(a) uses poison or drugs for any purpose in a manner that is likely to result in the death, injury, disabling, or capture of wildlife; or\n(b) has in his or her possession while hunting, poison or drugs that are commonly used for killing, injuring, disabling, or capturing wildlife.\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Use of poison and drugs",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s28",
   "number": "28",
   "text": "A person who wounds wildlife while hunting shall make a reasonable effort to kill it.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Wounding",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s29",
   "number": "29",
   "text": "(1) A person who has killed a game bird, big game animal, fur bearing animal or small game animal shall make a reasonable effort to retrieve it.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Retrieval",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s30",
   "number": "30",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not possess wildlife that has been killed, injured, disabled, or captured contrary to this Act.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a person issued a permit in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Illegally killed wildlife",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s31",
   "number": "31",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not have in his or her possession a greater number of species or types of wildlife, or parts of such wildlife, than he or she is permitted to possess under this Act.\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), a person shall not, without a permit, possess dead wildlife that he or she has come upon unexpectedly or discovered by chance.\n(3) A person may possess dead wildlife referred to in subsection (2) without a permit for only that period of time which is reasonably necessary to deliver the wildlife to a conservation officer.\n(4) A person who delivers wildlife to a conservation officer under subsection (3) may apply to the Minister for its return in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Possession Limits",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s32",
   "number": "32",
   "text": "(1) No person who has possession of a dead game bird, big game animal or small game animal shall allow any of the meat to be wasted.\n(2) For the purposes of this section, “meat” does not include the hide, head or viscera of a game bird, big game animal, or small game animal.\n(3) A person shall be deemed to have allowed meat to be wasted if that person allows any portion of a game bird, big game animal, or small game animal that is reasonably suitable for human consumption to be\n(a) fed to dogs or other domestic animals, or to wildlife in captivity;\n(b) destroyed or to become spoiled;\n(c) abandoned;\n(d) used for bait; or\n(e) left in the field without being properly dressed and cared for to prevent the meat from being scavenged or spoiled.\n(4) The regulations may prescribe the circumstances in which meat shall be deemed to be abandoned under paragraph (3)(c).\n(5) Subsections (1) and (3) do not apply in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Waste of meat",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s33",
   "number": "33",
   "text": "(1) A person who has killed a fur bearing animal shall not allow any part of the pelt to be wasted.\n(2) A person shall be deemed to have allowed part of a pelt to be wasted if the person\n(a) allows it to be destroyed or to become spoiled; or\n(b) abandons it.\n(3) The regulations may prescribe\n(a) the circumstances in which a pelt shall be deemed to be abandoned under paragraph (2)(b); and\n(b) other types or species of wildlife to which this section may apply.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Waste of pelt",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s34",
   "number": "34",
   "text": "(1) No person shall interfere intentionally with the hunting or trapping of any wildlife by a person who is authorized to hunt or trap the wildlife under this Act.\n(2) In cases in which it is proved that\n(a) a person interfered with the hunting or trapping of any wildlife by a person who is authorized to hunt or trap the wildlife under this Act; and\n(b) the person who interfered with the hunting or trapping made a public statement in the Yukon or elsewhere within six months before the interference that he or she intended to interfere with the hunting or trapping of wildlife in the Yukon,\nthe onus is on the person to prove that he or she did not intend to interfere with the hunting or trapping of wildlife on the occasion when he or she did so.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Interfering with hunting or trapping",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s35",
   "number": "35",
   "text": "If any wildlife or any part of any wildlife is found in a vehicle or boat it shall be deemed, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, to be in the possession of the operator of the vehicle or boat. If the identity of the operator is not proved, it shall be deemed to be in the possession of the registered owner or other person lawfully entitled to the use and possession of the vehicle or boat.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Wildlife in vehicles",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s36",
   "number": "36",
   "text": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a person has anything in his or her possession if the person has it in their personal possession or knowingly\n(a) has it in the actual possession or custody of another person; or\n(b) has it in any place, whether or not the place belongs to or is occupied by the person, for the use or benefit of that person or another.\n(2) For the purposes of this Act, if one of two or more persons, with the knowledge and consent of the rest, has anything in his or her custody or possession, it shall be deemed to be in the custody and possession of each and all of them.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Possession defined",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s37",
   "number": "37",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not hunt or trap wildlife in a wildlife sanctuary.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 1 — General Rules for Hunting and Trapping",
   "heading": "Wildlife sanctuaries",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s38",
   "number": "38",
   "text": "(1) No person who is not an outfitter shall provide or offer to provide or enter into a contract to provide a guide to any person for hunting big game animals.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a person\n(a) acting as a special guide under the authority of a special guiding licence issued under section 59; or\n(b) holding a big game guiding permit issued under section 58.\n(3) Despite subsection (1), if the Minister receives a request from an outfitter in the form determined by the Minister, the Minister shall issue a permit to the outfitter and to an eligible corporation named by the outfitter in the request, authorizing the outfitter and the corporation, in the name of the corporation\n(a) to offer to provide a guide to a person for hunting a big game animal; and\n(b) to provide a guide or enter into a contract to provide a guide, to a person for hunting a big game animal.\n(4) In subsection (3), “eligible corporation” means a corporation\n(a) that is in good standing under the Business Corporations Act;\n(b) that has the corporate power and capacity to provide the services of a guide for hunting big game animals;\n(c) of which the outfitter is a director;\n(d) that does not already hold a permit issued under subsection (3) which is still in effect; and\n(e) that meets any other qualifications prescribed by the regulations.\n(5) For the purposes authorized under subsection (3), an outfitter shall not use a name which is different than the name specified by the outfitter in the request.\n(6) A corporation issued a permit under subsection (3) shall not offer to provide a guide or provide a guide or enter into a contract to provide a guide at any time when the outfitter is not authorized to do so under this Act, the outfitter's outfitting concession or operating certificate.\n(7) The authorized use of a corporation under subsection (3) does not affect in any way the duties, responsibilities, or liabilities of an outfitter under this Act, an outfitting concession, or operating certificate, and for greater certainty, the outfitter is personally liable for a contravention of this Act by the corporation to the same extent as if the contravention had been committed by the outfitter.\n(8) A permit issued under subsection (3) is cancelled when one of the following occurs\n(a) the corporation is no longer an eligible corporation within the meaning of subsection (4);\n(b) the corporation holding the permit amalgamates or merges with another corporation;\n(c) the corporation is liquidated or dissolved, or is determined to be insolvent;\n(d) the Supreme Court makes an order for reorganization within the meaning of the Business Corporations Act;\n(e) the outfitting concession or operating certificate of the outfitter is revoked or cancelled; or\n(f) any other circumstance prescribed by the regulations.\n(9) An outfitter shall notify the Minister in writing immediately of the occurrence of any of the events described in paragraphs (8)(a) to (d) but failure of the outfitter to do so shall not affect the effective date of the cancellation of the permit.\n(10) A permit issued under subsection (3) is automatically suspended\n(a) if the outfitting concession or operating certificate is suspended under this Act; or\n(b) in such other circumstances prescribed by the regulations.\n(11) A guide or any other person employed or retained by or acting on behalf of the outfitter, including anyone employed or retained by or acting on behalf of a corporation issued a permit under subsection (3), shall not contravene the terms of the outfitter’s outfitting concession or operating certificate.",
   "part": "Part 2 — Outfitting, Guiding, and Trapping",
   "heading": "Guiding non-resident hunters",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)",
   "division": "Division 1 — Outfitting and Hunting"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s39",
   "number": "39",
   "text": "An outfitter shall not provide a guide to a person for hunting big game animals in an area in relation to which the outfitter is not authorized to provide a guide under sections 56 or 58.",
   "part": "Part 2 — Outfitting, Guiding, and Trapping",
   "heading": "Outfitting areas",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)",
   "division": "Division 1 — Outfitting and Hunting"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s40",
   "number": "40",
   "text": "(1) A non-resident shall not hunt a big game animal unless the non-resident\n(a) is accompanied by a guide provided by an outfitter;\n(b) is accompanied by a guide provided by the holder of a big game guiding permit; or\n(c) is a Canadian citizen or permanent resident and is accompanied by a person holding a special guide licence.\n(2) The prohibition in subsection (1) does not apply to an Inuvialuk who is hunting or trapping wildlife on the Yukon North Slope and whose hunting or trapping is governed by Part 13.",
   "part": "Part 2 — Outfitting, Guiding, and Trapping",
   "heading": "Non-residents and big game",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)",
   "division": "Division 1 — Outfitting and Hunting"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s41",
   "number": "41",
   "text": "(1) An outfitter shall provide each hunter with a separate guide to accompany the hunter while he or she is hunting big game animals.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 2 — Outfitting, Guiding, and Trapping",
   "heading": "Guides required",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)",
   "division": "Division 1 — Outfitting and Hunting"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s42",
   "number": "42",
   "text": "(1) Except under the authority of a guide licence, a person shall not\n(a) accompany any person in the field for compensation, reward, or gain, whether received or promised, to assist the person in hunting any big game animal; or\n(b) accompany a non-resident in the field to assist the non-resident in hunting any big game animal.\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), a person is deemed to be acting as a guide and is required to be a guide if he or she accompanies another person in the field in the manner described in subsection (1).\n(3) Paragraph (1)(b) does not apply to a person authorized by a special guide licence to accompany a non-resident hunting a big game animal.\n(4) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), an Inuvialuk who is hunting wildlife on the Yukon North Slope and whose hunting is governed by Part 13 is a resident.\n(5) An outfitter shall not employ, retain or provide a person to guide for the hunting of big game animals unless that person holds a guide licence issued under this Act.",
   "part": "Part 2 — Outfitting, Guiding, and Trapping",
   "heading": "Guiding activities",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)",
   "division": "Division 1 — Outfitting and Hunting"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s43",
   "number": "43",
   "text": "A guide shall not accompany a person in the field while the person is hunting for any species or type of big game animal unless the person has produced for the inspection of the guide a valid licence authorizing that person to hunt for that species or type of big game animal.",
   "part": "Part 2 — Outfitting, Guiding, and Trapping",
   "heading": "Hunter must have licence",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)",
   "division": "Division 1 — Outfitting and Hunting"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s44",
   "number": "44",
   "text": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), a guide shall not shoot at or near wildlife while acting as a guide.\n(2) A guide may, with the permission of the person for whom he or she is acting as a guide, shoot at a big game animal wounded by that person.\n(3) A guide has a reasonable responsibility\n(a) for the safety and well-being of the person he or she is guiding;\n(b) for the proper care and handling of any wildlife killed by the person he or she is guiding; and\n(c) for such other matters as may be prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 2 — Outfitting, Guiding, and Trapping",
   "heading": "Duties of guide",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)",
   "division": "Division 1 — Outfitting and Hunting"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s45",
   "number": "45",
   "text": "(1) For the purpose of ensuring compliance with this Act, a guide shall, on the request of a conservation officer, provide sufficient information to enable the officer to readily identify and locate the kill site of any wildlife hunted by a person\n(a) accompanied by the guide; or\n(b) while the guide was present.\n(2) If, in the opinion of a conservation officer, the information provided by a guide under subsection (1) may not be sufficient to readily identify and locate the kill site, the officer may require the guide to personally travel to the location of the kill site with the conservation officer, and the guide shall immediately comply with the officer’s requirement.",
   "part": "Part 2 — Outfitting, Guiding, and Trapping",
   "heading": "Kill site identification",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)",
   "division": "Division 1 — Outfitting and Hunting"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s46",
   "number": "46",
   "text": "A guide shall, without using force, make every reasonable effort to prevent a person he or she is guiding from committing a contravention of this Act.",
   "part": "Part 2 — Outfitting, Guiding, and Trapping",
   "heading": "Prevention of violations",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)",
   "division": "Division 1 — Outfitting and Hunting"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s47",
   "number": "47",
   "text": "(1) If a guide has reasonable grounds to believe that a contravention of this Act has been committed by a person accompanied by the guide, the guide shall mark the place and report the contravention as soon as practicable to the outfitter or to a conservation officer.\n(2) A guide’s report under subsection (1) shall include sufficient particulars to identify and locate the place where the contravention is believed to have occurred.\n(3) If a guide is required to report a contravention under subsection (1), the guide shall, on request, provide to a conservation officer such information relating to the contravention as the officer reasonably may require.",
   "part": "Part 2 — Outfitting, Guiding, and Trapping",
   "heading": "Report by Guide",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)",
   "division": "Division 1 — Outfitting and Hunting"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s48",
   "number": "48",
   "text": "(1) An outfitter has a duty to take all reasonable care to prevent a guide or other person employed or retained by, or acting on behalf of the outfitter, including a corporation which has been issued a permit under subsection 38(3), from contravening this Act, or the outfitter’s outfitting concession or operating certificate.\n(2) When a permit is issued to a corporation under subsection 38(3), the outfitter has a duty to take all reasonable care to ensure that any guide or other person employed or retained by or acting on behalf of the corporation in respect of the outfitter’s outfitting concession or operating certificate complies with this Act, the outfitting concession and the operating certificate.\n(3) An outfitter must be present in the Yukon during substantially all the times when persons are hunting in his or her outfitting concession area with guides provided by the outfitter.",
   "part": "Part 2 — Outfitting, Guiding, and Trapping",
   "heading": "Duties of outfitter",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)",
   "division": "Division 1 — Outfitting and Hunting"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s49",
   "number": "49",
   "text": "(1) If an outfitter has reasonable grounds to believe that a contravention of this Act has been committed by\n(a) a guide or other person employed or retained by or acting on behalf of the outfitter;\n(b) a guide or other person employed or retained by or acting on behalf of a corporation issued a permit under subsection 38(3); or\n(c) a client of the outfitter or a client of a corporation issued a permit under subsection 38(3),\nthe outfitter shall report the contravention to a conservation officer as soon as practicable and in any event within 48 hours.\n(2) If an outfitter is required to report a contravention under subsection (1), the outfitter shall, on request, provide to a conservation officer such information relating to the contravention as the officer reasonably may require.",
   "part": "Part 2 — Outfitting, Guiding, and Trapping",
   "heading": "Report by outfitter",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)",
   "division": "Division 1 — Outfitting and Hunting"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s50",
   "number": "50",
   "text": "(1) The Minister may issue an outfitting concession to an individual who\n(a) is a Canadian citizen or permanent resident;\n(b) ordinarily resides in Canada; and\n(c) meets any other qualifications prescribed by the regulations.\n(2) A person holding an outfitting concession shall not be issued another outfitting concession at any time a previously issued outfitting concession is in effect.\n(3) An outfitting concession is subject to the conditions prescribed by the regulations.\n(4) The Minister may, for the purposes of this Act, impose conditions in writing on an outfitting concession that do not conflict with this Act, including conditions imposed\n(a) for the purposes of ensuring compliance with this Act;\n(b) in the public interest to provide for the conservation of wildlife or for effective wildlife management; or\n(c) to establish quotas to limit the number of wildlife of any species or type that may be hunted by the clients of an outfitter.\n(5) A person issued an outfitting concession shall comply with any conditions of the concession.",
   "part": "Part 2 — Outfitting, Guiding, and Trapping",
   "heading": "Issuance of outfitting concession",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)",
   "division": "Division 1 — Outfitting and Hunting"
  },
  {
