   "id": "ykwildlife-s99",
   "number": "99",
   "text": "(1) A person who keeps wildlife in captivity shall ensure the wildlife\n(a) does not roam free;\n(b) does not escape from captivity; and\n(c) is not released to the wild.\n(2) If, despite subsection (1), wildlife escapes or is released from captivity, the person authorized under section 96 to keep wildlife in captivity shall\n(a) report the escape or release immediately to the Minister;\n(b) make all reasonable efforts to capture the wildlife as soon as practicable; and\n(c) provide such information as reasonably may be required by the Minister.\n(3) If the Minister is of the opinion that a person has not complied with paragraph (2)(b), the Minister may capture or kill the wildlife without incurring any liability.\n(4) The person authorized under section 96 to keep the wildlife in captivity is liable to the Minister for all expenses incurred by the Minister under subsection (3) unless the escape or release was caused by a natural disaster or an act of vandalism that was beyond the control of the person.\n(5) If wildlife in captivity escapes or is released and\n(a) damage is done to property by the wildlife or by anyone attempting to capture the wildlife; or\n(b) expense is reasonably incurred in attempting to capture or in maintaining or transporting the wildlife,\nthe person authorized to keep the wildlife in captivity is liable for that damage or expense, or both, unless it is due wholly to the fault of the person suffering the damage or expense.\n(6) In determining under subsection (5) whether liability for any damage or expense is assessable wholly against the person suffering the damage, a person is not wholly at fault only because he or she could have prevented the damage or expense by fencing his or her land.\n(7) A person is liable for any damage or expense referred to in subsection (5) if the person\n(a) opens and does not close or properly close a gate at a place licensed to keep wildlife in captivity; or\n(b) tampers with, damages, or destroys a gate or fence at a place licensed to keep wildlife in captivity\nand as a result wildlife is released or escapes from the place.\n(8) Nothing in subsection (7) restricts any liability under subsections (5) or (6).\n(9) The Government of the Yukon has a right of action under this section for damage or expense suffered by it.",
   "part": "Part 4 — Miscellaneous",
   "heading": "No escape or release of wildlife in captivity",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s100",
   "number": "100",
   "text": "Subject to section 139, nothing in this Act affects any rights or remedies a person has at common law or by statute for trespass to land.",
   "part": "Part 4 — Miscellaneous",
   "heading": "Trespass",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s101",
   "number": "101",
   "text": "(1) Subject to this Act, all property, rights, title and interest in and to wildlife are vested in the Crown.\n(2) Despite subsection (1) or any other provision of this or any other Act, no right of action lies, and no right of compensation exists, against the Crown for death, personal injury or property damage caused by any wildlife.",
   "part": "Part 4 — Miscellaneous",
   "heading": "Title to wildlife and Crown liability",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s102",
   "number": "102",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not traffic in wildlife or possess wildlife for the purpose of trafficking, except under the authority of a licence or permit and in accordance with this Act.\n(2) A person shall not sell any thing that the person represents as wildlife unless the person has a licence or permit to sell that wildlife.\n(3) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 4 — Miscellaneous",
   "heading": "No trafficking in wildlife",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s103",
   "number": "103",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not serve wildlife as food at any place where meals are served for or in the hope or expectation of remuneration.\n(2) A person shall not bring an edible part of wildlife into, or possess it in, any place where meals are served for or in the hope or expectation of remuneration.\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to a person issued a permit in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 4 — Miscellaneous",
   "heading": "Serving wildlife",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s104",
   "number": "104",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not import or transport live wildlife into the Yukon.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a person issued a permit in accordance with the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 4 — Miscellaneous",
   "heading": "Transporting or importing live wildlife into the Yukon",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s105",
   "number": "105",
   "text": "(1) Subject to section 203, a person shall not ship or transport any wildlife from the Yukon.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 4 — Miscellaneous",
   "heading": "Shipping or transporting wildlife from the Yukon",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s106",
   "number": "106",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not ship or transport, or deliver to another person for shipping or transporting, any wildlife captured or killed in contravention of this Act.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 4 — Miscellaneous",
   "heading": "Transporting wildlife killed contrary to this Act",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s107",
   "number": "107",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not possess wildlife that\n(a) was killed, captured, taken, possessed, transported, bought or sold contrary to the laws of another jurisdiction; or\n(b) was removed from another jurisdiction, contrary to the laws of that jurisdiction.\n(2) A person shall not sell or offer to sell wildlife that has been transported into the Yukon if the sale would not be permitted in the jurisdiction from which the wildlife was originally exported.\n(3) If a pelt is transported into the Yukon from a jurisdiction that requires the pelt to be sealed or marked, a person shall not remove the seal or mark or possess the pelt without the seal or mark.",
   "part": "Part 4 — Miscellaneous",
   "heading": "Laws of other jurisdictions",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s108",
   "number": "108",
   "text": "The Minister may issue licences and permits for the purposes of this Act.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Issuance of licences",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s109",
   "number": "109",
   "text": "(1) The Minister may authorize a person to issue licences and permits on the Minister’s behalf.\n(2) A person who is authorized under subsection (1) to issue licences or permits and who is not a member of the public service shall be paid the prescribed remuneration for each licence or permit the person issues.\n(3) A person who issues a licence or permit under this section is considered to be an agent of the Government of the Yukon for the collection of any fee required to be paid in respect of the issuance of the licence or permit, and sections 63 to 71 of the Financial Administration Act apply in respect of the fees collected by the person.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Issuers",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s110",
   "number": "110",
   "text": "A person who is authorized to issue licences or permits on the Minister’s behalf shall comply with any applicable manual of instructions issued by the Minister, as it may be amended from time to time.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Manual of instructions",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s111",
   "number": "111",
   "text": "A licence or permit is subject to the conditions prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Conditions by the regulations",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s112",
   "number": "112",
   "text": "The Minister may at any time impose written conditions on a licence or permit that do not conflict with this Act.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Conditions by the Minister",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s113",
   "number": "113",
   "text": "Every person to whom a licence or permit is issued shall comply with any conditions to which the licence or permit is subject under this Act.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Compliance with conditions",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s114",
   "number": "114",
   "text": "A person who is hunting, trapping, guiding or acting as a special guide shall carry on his or her person any licence or permit issued under this Act.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Licence or permit to be carried",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s115",
   "number": "115",
   "text": "On the request of a conservation officer, a person holding a licence, permit or operating certificate or purporting to do anything under the authority of a licence, permit or operating certificate shall produce and show it to the officer.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Producing licence to officer",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s116",
   "number": "116",
   "text": "(1) No person to whom a licence, permit or operating certificate has been issued shall deliver it to another person in circumstances where he or she might reasonably expect that the other person would\n(a) purport to a conservation officer to be the holder of the licence, permit or operating certificate; or\n(b) purport to exercise any authority or privileges granted by the licence, permit or operating certificate.\n(2) No person who is in possession of any licence, permit or operating certificate issued to another person shall purport to a conservation officer to be the holder of the licence, permit or operating certificate.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Transfer of licences, permits and operating certificates",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s117",
   "number": "117",
   "text": "A person shall not possess a licence or permit that\n(a) does not identify the holder of the licence or permit;\n(b) is dated earlier than its date of issuance; or\n(c) is incomplete in any material respect.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Incomplete licences and permits",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s118",
   "number": "118",
   "text": "(1) A person shall not, in providing any information required to be provided by or under this Act, or in answering any questions that the person is required to answer pursuant to a provision of this Act, make a false or misleading statement, or provide false or misleading information or fail to disclose a material fact.\n(2) A licence or permit issued to a person who has made a false or misleading representation to obtain the licence or permit is void unless the representation relates only to some matter that reasonably could not have influenced the decision to issue the licence or permit to that person.\n(3) When a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (1) in relation to a licence or permit and the false or misleading statement by the person reasonably could have influenced the decision to issue a licence or permit to the person, the person shall not apply for or obtain any such licence or permit in the following licensing year.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "False or misleading representations",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s119",
   "number": "119",
   "text": "A person shall not\n(a) deface or alter a licence, permit, operating certificate, outfitting concession or trapping concession; or\n(b) have in his or her possession\n(i) a document that purports to be but is not in fact a document described in paragraph (a), or\n(ii) a document described in paragraph (a) which has been defaced or altered.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Alteration without authority",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s120",
   "number": "120",
   "text": "A person shall not possess, use or display or cause or allow to be displayed a void licence or permit.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Use of void licence or permit",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s121",
   "number": "121",
   "text": "On the request of a conservation officer, a person shall surrender a licence or permit that is void or that the officer believes on reasonable grounds to be void.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Surrender of void licence or permit",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s122",
   "number": "122",
   "text": "(1) The Minister may refuse to issue a licence, permit or operating certificate for any cause that seems sufficient to the Minister.\n(2) The Minister may cancel or suspend any licence, permit or operating certificate for any cause that seems sufficient to the Minister.\n(3) If the Minister cancels or suspends a licence, permit or operating certificate, it may be reinstated on the conditions which the Minister considers advisable.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Refusal of licence, permit, or operating certificate",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s123",
   "number": "123",
   "text": "No person who is not a Yukon resident shall apply for or obtain a licence or permit that may be issued only to Yukon residents under this Act.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Non-residents",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s124",
   "number": "124",
   "text": "(1) A Yukon resident shall not apply for or obtain a licence or permit to hunt that may only be issued to a Yukon resident if they have been issued in another jurisdiction a type of licence or other authorization to hunt which may only be issued to a person who is a resident of that other jurisdiction and which licence or authorization is still in effect.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Licensed in another jurisdiction",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s125",
   "number": "125",
   "text": "(1) No licence or permit shall be issued to any corporation, society or other body that is not an individual.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a corporation referred to in subsection 38(3) or in the circumstances prescribed by the regulations.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "No licence to corporation",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s126",
   "number": "126",
   "text": "(1) A licence, permit, operating certificate, outfitting concession or trapping concession is not, and does not operate as a demise, lease or transfer of any title to or interest in land or wildlife.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not affect any rights or remedies a person has at common law or by statute, against any person for damages suffered as a result of interference with the operations of the person’s outfitting concession or trapping concession.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Title to land and wildlife",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s127",
   "number": "127",
   "text": "(1) In this section, “authorization” means\n(a) a guide licence;\n(b) an operating certificate;\n(c) an outfitting concession;\n(d) a trapping concession;\n(e) a licence to trap;\n(f) a big game guiding permit;\n(g) a taxidermy licence;\n(h) a game farm licence; or\n(i) any other licence or permit to which this section is prescribed by the regulations to apply.\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), if the Minister imposes conditions in writing on an authorization, the person issued the authorization may, not later than 10 days after the conditions are imposed, give the Minister written notice of disagreement with the conditions.\n(3) This section does not apply to an authorization or the person holding an authorization if the conditions imposed by the Minister are the same as conditions which were imposed by the Minister in a previous authorization issued to that person, for which that person requested a hearing under subsection (9), following which the Concession and Compensation Review Board issued a report which was considered by the Minister under subsection (12).\n(4) A person holding an authorization who gives a notice of disagreement may carry out the activities permitted by the authorization, subject to the conditions, without prejudice to a hearing under subsection (9) or to the decision of the Minister under subsection (12).\n(5) When the Minister receives a notice of disagreement under subsection (2), the Minister shall serve a notice of receipt on the person giving the notice of disagreement.\n(6) A notice served by the Minister under subsection (5) shall be served personally or by registered mail addressed to the person to be served at the person’s last known address.\n(7) Notice served by registered mail shall be considered to have been served on the seventh day after the day of mailing, unless the person served establishes that he or she did not, acting in good faith, through absence, accident, illness or other cause beyond the person’s control, receive the notice until a later date.\n(8) A notice served under subsection (5) shall inform the person to whom the notice is given that the person may require a hearing by mailing or delivering a written request for a hearing to the Minister within 15 days after the service of notice.\n(9) If the Minister receives a request for a hearing in accordance with subsection (8), the Minister shall refer the matter to the Concession and Compensation Review Board to hold a hearing and to report to the Minister as provided for under subsection (11).\n(10) The person who requested the hearing and the Minister are entitled to be heard at the hearing.\n(11) After the hearing, the Concession and Compensation Review Board shall issue a report to the Minister that contains\n(a) a summary of the evidence presented at the hearing;\n(b) the Board’s opinion on the merits of the conditions imposed by the Minister on the authorization, having regard to\n(i) what is reasonably necessary for the conservation and management of wildlife,\n(ii) the effective administration of this Act, and\n(iii) ensuring compliance with this Act; and\n(c) the reasons for the board’s opinion.\n(12) After considering the Concession and Compensation Review Board’s report, the Minister may confirm the conditions he or she imposed on the authorization or decide to remove or amend them.",
   "part": "Part 5 — Licences",
   "heading": "Condition Review Process",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s128",
   "number": "128",
   "text": "(1) The Minister may designate a person or class of persons as conservation officers for the purposes of this Act, and a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police is a conservation officer for the purposes of this Act.\n(2) The Minister may place terms or conditions on a designation under subsection (1).\n(3) Subject to subsection (2), every conservation officer has the authority to enforce provisions of this Act.\n(4) A conservation officer is a peace officer within the meaning of the Criminal Code (Canada) for the purposes of enforcing this Act and, subject to subsection (2), has the powers and protections provided by law to a peace officer.",
   "part": "Part 6 — Conservation Officers and Wildlife Technicians",
   "heading": "Conservation officers",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s129",
   "number": "129",
   "text": "(1) The Minister may designate a person or class of persons as wildlife technicians for the purposes of this Act.\n(2) The Minister may place terms or conditions on a designation under subsection (1).",
   "part": "Part 6 — Conservation Officers and Wildlife Technicians",
   "heading": "Wildlife Technicians",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s130",
   "number": "130",
   "text": "The Minister may, in writing, authorize a conservation officer or wildlife technician to do, in the execution of his or her duties under this Act, an act the doing of which otherwise constitutes a contravention of this Act.",
   "part": "Part 6 — Conservation Officers and Wildlife Technicians",
   "heading": "Official authorization",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s131",
   "number": "131",
   "text": "Without limiting the generality of section 130, conservation officers or wildlife technicians may, if they are authorized in writing by the Minister to do so in the execution of their duties, hunt or trap any wildlife that is required for the purpose of wildlife management or research.",
   "part": "Part 6 — Conservation Officers and Wildlife Technicians",
   "heading": "Wildlife studies",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s132",
   "number": "132",
   "text": "Despite any other provision of this Act, conservation officers or wildlife technicians may hunt or trap at any time and at any place wildlife that they believe, on reasonable grounds, is dangerous, destructive, wounded or diseased.",
   "part": "Part 6 — Conservation Officers and Wildlife Technicians",
   "heading": "Dangerous wildlife",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s133",
   "number": "133",
   "text": "A person shall not\n(a) knowingly make a false or misleading statement to a conservation officer or wildlife technician who is acting under this Act; or\n(b) obstruct or interfere with a conservation officer or wildlife technician who is acting under this Act.",
   "part": "Part 6 — Conservation Officers and Wildlife Technicians",
   "heading": "Obstruction of officer",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s134",
   "number": "134",
   "text": "An oath, affidavit, affirmation or statutory declaration under this Act may be administered, sworn, affirmed or made before a conservation officer.",
   "part": "Part 6 — Conservation Officers and Wildlife Technicians",
   "heading": "Oaths",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s135",
   "number": "135",
   "text": "A conservation officer who is acting under this Part shall, upon request, produce his or her badge or other identification.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Production of identification",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s136",
   "number": "136",
   "text": "(1) For the purposes of ensuring compliance with this Act or to enforce any provision of this Act, a conservation officer may signal or otherwise direct the operator of a vehicle or boat to stop it or move it to a place and stop it and the operator shall immediately comply with the conservation officer’s signal or direction and shall not proceed for the time that is reasonably necessary for the officer to conduct any lawful inquiries.\n(2) The operator and any occupants of a vehicle or boat stopped under subsection (1) shall promptly produce for inspection any wildlife, firearm, licence, permit or other thing requested by the officer relating to this Act.\n(3) For the purposes of subsection (1), signals to stop include intermittent flashes of red or blue light, a hand signal, an audible request, a siren, or other sign to stop.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Stopping vehicles and boats",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s137",
   "number": "137",
   "text": "(1) For the purposes of ensuring compliance with this Act, or to enforce any provisions of this Act, a conservation officer may signal or otherwise direct a person\n(a) riding or leading a pack animal; or\n(b) carrying a pack, or a firearm in plain view\nin an area usually inhabited by wildlife to stop, or to move to a place and then stop, and the person shall immediately comply with the conservation officer’s signal or direction and shall not proceed for the time that is reasonably necessary to enable the officer to conduct any lawful inquiries.\n(2) A person stopped under subsection (1) shall produce for inspection any wildlife, firearm, licence, permit or other thing requested by the officer relating to this Act.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Stopping persons on pack animals and carrying packs or firearms",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s138",
   "number": "138",
   "text": "(1) For the purposes of ensuring compliance with this Act, a conservation officer and any person assisting the officer may, subject to subsection (2), at any reasonable time enter and inspect any building or other place in which the officer believes on reasonable grounds there is any thing to which this Act applies or any document relating to the administration of this Act.\n(2) A conservation officer may not enter a dwelling house except with the consent of the occupant or person in charge of the dwelling house or under the authority of a warrant.\n(3) In carrying out an inspection under this section a conservation officer may\n(a) open or cause to be opened any container or receptacle that the conservation officer believes on reasonable grounds contains any thing or document referred to in subsection (1);\n(b) inspect the thing and take samples free of charge;\n(c) require any person to produce the document for inspection or copying, in whole or in part;\n(d) ask questions that may be relevant to the inspection;\n(e) inspect any other thing that is in the building or place to which this Act applies;\n(f) use or cause to be used any computer system for the purpose of examining information contained in or available to the system, and reproduce any record or cause it to be reproduced from the data in the form of a printout or other intelligible output;\n(g) remove any documents or things for the purpose of making copies or for further inspection, but the copying or further inspection shall be carried out with reasonable dispatch and the documents or things shall be returned promptly to the person from whom they were taken;\n(h) use or cause to be used any copying equipment at the place to make copies of any documents or records inspected or produced during the inspection; and\n(i) seize any thing or document by means of or in relation to which the conservation officer believes, on reasonable grounds, this Act has been contravened or that the officer believes, on reasonable grounds, will provide evidence of a contravention.\n(4) A person shall during the inspection provide information requested by the conservation officer that is relevant to the inspection.\n(5) Every person who is in possession or control of a building or other place being inspected under this section must permit the conservation officer to do anything referred to in subsection (3).\n(6) On an ex parte application, a justice may issue a warrant in the prescribed form, subject to any conditions specified in it, authorizing a conservation officer and any other persons or class of persons named in it to enter a dwelling house, if the justice is satisfied by information on oath in the prescribed form that\n(a) the conditions for entry described in subsection (1) exist in relation to the dwelling house;\n(b) entry into the dwelling house is necessary for the purposes of administration of this Act; and\n(c) entry to the dwelling house has been refused or there are reasonable grounds for believing that entry will be refused.\n(7) In executing a warrant issued under subsection (6), a conservation officer may not use force unless the use of force has been specifically authorized in the warrant.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Inspecting buildings and other places",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s139",
   "number": "139",
   "text": "In the performance of their duties under this Act, a conservation officer or wildlife technician, and any person assisting them, may enter upon any land, and while doing this, they are liable only for any actual damage willfully or negligently caused by them.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Entry upon land",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s140",
   "number": "140",
   "text": "(1) A conservation officer may at any reasonable time require persons who have, within the 12 months immediately preceding, operated an aircraft in the Yukon for the transportation of wildlife, or for the transportation of persons in connection with the hunting or trapping of wildlife, to produce for the inspection of the officer any log books and other records in their possession pertaining to the flight.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply in respect of the operation of an aircraft by a commercial airline company on a regularly scheduled flight directly from one airport to another.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Aircraft log books and records",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s141",
   "number": "141",
   "text": "(1) When on ex parte application a justice is satisfied by information on oath in the prescribed form that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in a building, receptacle, or other place\n(a) anything on or in respect of which an offence against this Act has been or is suspected to have been committed;\n(b) anything that there are reasonable grounds to believe will afford evidence with respect to the commission of an offence against this Act; or\n(c) anything that will reveal the whereabouts of a person who is believed to have committed an offence against this Act,\nthe justice may issue a warrant in the prescribed form subject to any terms or conditions the justice considers necessary, authorizing a conservation officer and any other persons or class of persons named therein to search the building, receptacle or place for any thing and to seize it.\n(2) A search warrant issued under this section shall name a date on which it expires, which date shall be not later than fifteen days after its issue.\n(3) A search warrant issued under this section shall be executed by day, unless\n(a) the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for it to be executed by night;\n(b) the reasonable grounds are included in the information; and\n(c) the warrant authorizes that it be executed by night.\n(4) A person authorized under this section to search a computer system in a building or place for data may\n(a) use or cause to be used any computer system at the building or place to search any data contained in or available to the computer system;\n(b) reproduce or cause to be reproduced any data in the form of a print-out or other intelligible output;\n(c) seize the print-out or other intelligible output; and\n(d) use or cause to be used any computing equipment at the place to make copies of the data.\n(5) Every person who is in possession or control of any building or place in respect of which a search is carried out under this section shall, on presentation of the warrant or on the request of a conservation officer acting under subsection 142(1), permit the person carrying out the search\n(a) to use or cause to be used any computer system at the building or place in order to search any data contained in or available to the computer system for data that the person is authorized by this section to search for;\n(b) to obtain a hard copy of the data and to seize it; and\n(c) to use or cause to be used any copying equipment at the place to make copies of the data.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Searches with a warrant",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s142",
   "number": "142",
   "text": "(1) A conservation officer may exercise the powers of search and seizure described in subsection 141(1) without a warrant if the conditions for obtaining a warrant exist but, by reason of exigent circumstances, it would not be feasible to obtain a warrant.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a dwelling house.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Searches without a warrant",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s143",
   "number": "143",
   "text": "(1) If, on ex parte application, a Territorial Court judge or a judge of the Supreme Court is satisfied by information on oath in the prescribed form that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence against this Act has been or will be committed, and that information concerning the offence will be obtained through the use of a technique, procedure, device, or the doing of the thing described in the information, the judge may issue a warrant authorizing a conservation officer identified in the warrant and any other person named therein to use any device or investigative technique or procedure or do any thing described in the warrant that would if not authorized, constitute an unreasonable search or seizure in respect of a person or a person's property.\n(2) Section 487.01 of the Criminal Code (Canada) applies to a warrant issued under subsection (1), with such modifications as the circumstances require.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Warrant to use technique, device, etc.",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s144",
   "number": "144",
   "text": "When a conservation officer believes it would be impracticable to appear personally to make an application for a warrant under sections 141 or 143, a warrant may be issued under those sections on an information submitted by telephone or other means of telecommunication in the manner provided for under section 487.1 of the Criminal Code (Canada) with such modifications as the circumstances require.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Telewarrant",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s145",
   "number": "145",
   "text": "A conservation officer may use as much force as is necessary to execute a search warrant issued under sections 141 or 143, or to exercise any authority given by section 142.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Use of force",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s146",
   "number": "146",
   "text": "(1) A conservation officer who is lawfully in a building or other place may, without a warrant, seize any thing that he or she believes on reasonable grounds\n(a) has been obtained by the commission of an offence under this Act;\n(b) has been used in the commission of an offence under this Act;\n(c) will afford evidence of the commission of an offence under this Act; or\n(d) is intermixed with a thing referred to in paragraphs (a), (b) or (c ).\n(2) If a conservation officer is in a building or other place pursuant to a warrant, subsection (1) applies to any thing, whether or not it is specified in the warrant.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Seizures without a warrant",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s147",
   "number": "147",
   "text": "(1) When a conservation officer seizes a thing in the execution of a warrant issued under this Act the officer shall, as soon as practicable, bring the thing seized before a justice, or report to a justice that the thing has been seized.\n(2) When a conservation officer in the execution of duties under this Act seizes a thing without a warrant, other than wildlife, the officer shall, as soon as practicable, bring the thing seized before a justice, or report to a justice that the thing has been seized.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Report to a Justice",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s148",
   "number": "148",
   "text": "(1) If a conservation officer in the execution of duties under this Act seizes wildlife without a warrant, the person from whom the wildlife was seized or any other person claiming lawful entitlement to possession of the wildlife may apply to a justice in the prescribed form within thirty days after the seizure for return or release of the wildlife.\n(2) If no application is made under subsection (1) within thirty days of the seizure, the wildlife is forfeited to the Government of the Yukon.\n(3) If the lawful ownership of or the identity of the person from whom a thing was seized, with or without a warrant, has not been ascertained within 30 days after the seizure, the thing is forfeited to the Government of the Yukon.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Application for return of wildlife seized without warrant",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s149",
   "number": "149",
   "text": "A conservation officer may at any time take, for examination or testing, samples of any wildlife seized under this Act, and such samples are forfeited to the Government of the Yukon.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Samples of seized wildlife",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s150",
   "number": "150",
   "text": "Despite subsections 147(1) and 148(1), any dead wildlife that is seized is forfeited to the Government of the Yukon if, in the opinion of the conservation officer, it is not practicable to maintain the wildlife in custody or it is likely to spoil or otherwise perish.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Forfeiture of dead wildlife",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s151",
   "number": "151",
   "text": "Despite subsections 147(1) and 148(1) any live wildlife that is seized is forfeited to the Government of the Yukon if, in the opinion of the conservation officer, it is not practicable to maintain the wildlife in custody.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Forfeiture of live wildlife",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s152",
   "number": "152",
   "text": "(1) Despite subsections 147(1), 147(2), 148(1) and section 2.01 of the Summary Convictions Act, a thing seized shall not be ordered or otherwise returned to any person if the use or possession of the thing is an offence under this Act, and the thing shall be forfeited to the Government of the Yukon.\n(2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not a charge is laid in respect of the thing seized, and if a charge is laid, subsection (1) applies even if the defendant is acquitted or the charge is withdrawn or stayed.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Forfeiture if use or possession is an offence",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s153",
   "number": "153",
   "text": "A thing forfeited to the Government of the Yukon under this Act shall be disposed of in accordance with the directions of the Minister.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Disposal of things forfeited",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s154",
   "number": "154",
   "text": "The lawful owner and any person lawfully entitled to possession of any thing seized or forfeited under this Act are jointly and severally liable for all costs of inspection, seizure, forfeiture or disposition incurred by the Government of the Yukon that exceed any proceeds of the disposition of the thing that was forfeited to the Government of the Yukon under this Act.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Owner liable for costs of inspection, seizure, etc.",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s155",
   "number": "155",
   "text": "No liability attaches to the Government of the Yukon, to the Minister, to a conservation officer or to a wildlife technician for loss or damage arising from the seizure, disposal or return in accordance with this Act of anything that has been seized, or from the deterioration of anything while it is being held under a seizure, other than loss or damage resulting from negligence or willful neglect in its care, custody or return.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Liability for seized things",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s156",
   "number": "156",
   "text": "(1) A conservation officer may arrest without warrant a person the officer believes on reasonable grounds\n(a) is committing an offence under this Act; or\n(b) has committed or is about to commit an offence under this Act and by reason of exigent circumstances it would be impracticable to obtain a warrant to arrest the person.\n(2) A conservation officer who arrests a person under this section shall, as soon as practicable, release the person from custody unless the officer believes on reasonable grounds that it is necessary in the public interest for the person to be detained, having regard to all the circumstances, including the need to\n(a) establish the identity of the person;\n(b) preserve or secure evidence of or relating to the offence;\n(c) prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence or the commission of another offence; or\n(d) ensure that the person will attend court to be dealt with according to law.\n(3) A person detained under subsection (2) shall be brought before a justice as soon as practicable, and in any event within 24 hours, to be dealt with by the justice according to law.\n(4) A conservation officer may use as much force as is necessary to make an arrest under this section.",
   "part": "Part 7 — Enforcement",
   "heading": "Arrest",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s157",
   "number": "157",
   "text": "(1) A person who contravenes any provision of this Act is guilty of an offence.\n(2) A person who fails to comply with an order of a court made under this Act is guilty of an offence.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Offences",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s158",
   "number": "158",
   "text": "If a corporation commits an offence under this Act, an officer, director, employee or agent of the corporation who directed, authorized, assented to, acquiesced in or participated in the commission of the offence is party to and guilty of the offence and is liable on conviction to the punishment provided for the offence, whether or not the corporation has been prosecuted for the offence.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Corporations",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s159",
   "number": "159",
   "text": "A defendant may be convicted of an offence under this Act if it is established that the offence was committed by an employee or agent of the defendant, whether or not the employee or agent is identified or has been prosecuted for the offence.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Employers and principals",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s160",
   "number": "160",
   "text": "A defendant may be convicted of an offence under this Act if it is established that the offence was committed by a person in the course of operations under a licence or permit issued to the defendant, whether or not the person is identified or has been prosecuted for the offence.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Licensees and permittees",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s161",
   "number": "161",
   "text": "(1) A person convicted of an offence under this Act is liable to a fine of not more than $50,000, to imprisonment for a term of not more than one year, or to both.\n(2) Despite subsection (1), a person convicted of an offence under this Act is liable to a fine of not more than $100,000, to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years, or to both, if\n(a) the offence was committed for a commercial purpose or to otherwise obtain, directly or indirectly, a monetary benefit, whether received or promised; or\n(b) the offence relates to specially protected wildlife.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Fines and penalties",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s162",
   "number": "162",
   "text": "If a person is convicted of an offence under this Act a second or subsequent time, the amount of the fine for the subsequent offence may, despite section 161, be double the amount set out in that section.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Fines for second and subsequent offences",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s163",
   "number": "163",
   "text": "If an offence under this Act is committed on more than one day or is continued for more than one day, the offence is considered to be a separate offence for each day on which the offence is committed or continued.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Continuing offences",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s164",
   "number": "164",
   "text": "Despite section 161, any fine imposed on a conviction for an offence involving more than one animal may be calculated in respect of each animal as though it had been the subject of a separate complaint or information.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Cumulative fines",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s165",
   "number": "165",
   "text": "When a person is convicted of an offence under this Act and the court is satisfied that monetary benefits accrued directly or indirectly to the person as a result of the commission of the offence, the court may order the person to pay an additional fine in an amount equal to the court’s estimation of the amount of the monetary benefits, which additional fine may exceed the maximum amount of any fine that may otherwise be imposed under this Act.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Additional fine for value of monetary benefits",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s166",
   "number": "166",
   "text": "If a person is convicted of an offence and a fine is imposed,\n(a) a thing seized in connection with the offence and not forfeited to the Government of the Yukon under this Act shall not be returned until the fine has been paid; and\n(b) if the fine is not paid and is considered to be a debt due under the Summary Convictions Act, a justice may order that the thing be forfeited to the Government of the Yukon.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Unpaid fines",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s167",
   "number": "167",
   "text": "(1) If a person is convicted of an offence under this Act, the justice may order that any thing seized in connection with the offence be forfeited to the Government of the Yukon.\n(2) Subsection (1) applies in addition to any other penalty.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Forfeiture after conviction",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s168",
   "number": "168",
   "text": "If a person is convicted of an offence under this Act, the justice may, in addition to any other penalty, order the person to pay all or part of any expenses incurred by the Minister with respect to the seizure, storage or disposition of any thing seized in connection with the offence.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Order to pay expenses",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s169",
   "number": "169",
   "text": "(1) If a person is convicted of an offence under this Act, in addition to any punishment imposed, the court may, having regard to the nature of the offence and the circumstances surrounding its commission, make an order containing any one or more of the following prohibitions, directions or requirements\n(a) prohibiting the person for a period of time specified in the order, from possessing wildlife, or from doing any act or engaging in any activity that could, in the opinion of the court, result in the continuation or repetition of the offence;\n(b) directing the person to take any action the court considers appropriate to remedy or avoid any harm to wildlife or its habitat that resulted or may result from the commission of the offence;\n(c) directing the person to publish, in any manner the court considers appropriate, the facts relating to the commission of the offence;\n(d) directing the person to pay to the Government of the Yukon an amount of money as compensation for all or part of the cost of any remedial or preventative action taken by or caused to be taken on behalf of the Government of the Yukon as a result of the commission of the offence;\n(e) directing the person to perform community service in accordance with any reasonable conditions that may be specified in the order;\n(f) directing the person to submit to the Minister, on application to the court by the Minister within three years after the date of the conviction, any information about the activities of the person in relation to matters within the scope of this Act that the court considers appropriate in the circumstances;\n(g) directing the person to post a bond or pay money into court for the purpose of ensuring compliance with any prohibition, direction or requirement under this section;\n(h) directing the person to pay an amount of money the court considers appropriate to the Conservation Fund established under section 186;\n(i) requiring the person to successfully complete a hunter education course and successfully pass an examination for applicants for licences to hunt before the person applies for a licence to hunt; or\n(j) requiring the person to comply with any other conditions that the court considers appropriate for securing the person’s good conduct and for preventing the person from repeating the offence or committing other offences against this Act.\n(2) The court may direct that moneys paid to the Conservation Fund under paragraph 1(h) be contributed by the Fund to a violation reporting system.\n(3) If a person fails to comply with an order referred to in paragraph (1)(c) directing the person to publish the facts relating to the commission of the offence, the Minister may publish those facts and recover the costs of publication from the person.\n(4) If the Minister incurs publication costs under subsection (3), the amount of the costs and the interest payable by law on the costs constitute a debt due to the Government of the Yukon and may be recovered as such in a court of competent jurisdiction.\n(5) If an order is made under paragraph (1)(h) directing a person to pay money, the amount due and any interest payable on that amount constitute a debt due to the Government of the Yukon in trust for the Conservation Fund and the debt due may be recovered as such in any court of competent jurisdiction.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Additional court orders",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s170",
   "number": "170",
   "text": "(1) An application for variation of an order under section 169 may be made to the court that made the order by the prosecution or by the person to whom the order is directed.\n(2) Before hearing an application under subsection (1), the court may order the applicant to give notice of the application in accordance with directions of the court.\n(3) On application under subsection (1), if the court considers variation appropriate because of a material change in circumstances, the court may make an order doing one or more of the following\n(a) changing the original order or any conditions in it;\n(b) relieving the person to whom the order is directed, either absolutely or partially or for any period of time the court considers appropriate, from any prohibition, direction or requirement in the original order;\n(c) reducing the period for which the original order is to remain in effect; or\n(d) extending the period for which the original order is to remain in effect, subject to the limit that this extension must not be longer than one year.\n(4) If an application has been heard by the court under subsection (1), no other application may be made in respect of the same order except with the leave of the court.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Variation of order",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s171",
   "number": "171",
   "text": "(1) If a person is convicted of an offence under this Act and the court suspends the passing of sentence, the court may, in addition to any probation order, make an order directing the person to comply with any prohibition, direction or requirement referred to in subsection 169(1).\n(2) If a person whose sentence has been suspended fails to comply with an order made under subsection 169(1) or is convicted, within three years after the day on which the order was made, of another offence under this Act, the court may, on the application of the prosecution, impose any sentence that could have been imposed if the passing of sentence had not been suspended.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Orders under suspended sentence",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s172",
   "number": "172",
   "text": "(1) If a person is convicted of an offence referred to in subsection (2),\n(a) every licence or permit authorizing that person to hunt any species or type of wildlife is cancelled; and\n(b) that person shall not possess, apply for or obtain any licence or permit authorizing the person to hunt, in the immediately following licensing year, any species or type of wildlife.\n(2) Subsection (1) applies to\n(a) an offence under sections 11, 12, 20, 22, 123, 133 and subsections 8(1), 8(2), 21(1), 24(1), 25(1), 27(1), 37(1), 38(1), 40(1) and 42(1); and\n(b) an offence prescribed by the regulations as an offence to which this section applies.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Automatic Cancellation",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s173",
   "number": "173",
   "text": "(1) If a person is convicted of an offence under this Act, the Migratory Birds Convention Act, 1994 (Canada) or the Wild Animal Plant Protection and Regulation of International and Interprovincial Trade Act (Canada), in addition to any penalty under subsection 172(1), the court may order that during a period specified in the order\n(a) the person shall not possess, apply for or obtain a licence or permit of a kind that is related to the offence, as specified by the court; and\n(b) the person shall not engage in any activity for which the person would be required to hold a licence or permit of the kind specified under paragraph (a).\n(2) If a court makes an order under subsection (1) in respect of a kind of licence or permit\n(a) that the person holds at the time the order is made; and\n(b) which is not cancelled under paragraph 172(1)(a)\nthe court shall order that the licence or permit be cancelled.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Order not to obtain licence or permit",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s174",
   "number": "174",
   "text": "An appeal of a conviction or sentence does not\n(a) affect the cancellation of a licence or permit under paragraph 172(1)(a);\n(b) affect the prohibition under paragraph 172(1)(b) against possessing, applying for, or obtaining a licence or permit; or\n(c) stay the effect of an order under section 173.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Appeal does not stay order",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s175",
   "number": "175",
   "text": "(1) Within seven days after learning of its cancellation or suspension, the holder of a licence, permit or operating certificate shall surrender it to a conservation officer.\n(2) If a licence, permit or operating certificate is cancelled, suspended, or a new one ordered not to be issued, the person shall not obtain or attempt to obtain a replacement or newly issued licence, permit or operating certificate during the period that the cancellation, suspension or period of non-issuance is in force.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Surrender of licence and replacement",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s176",
   "number": "176",
   "text": "If a licence, permit or operating certificate is cancelled, suspended or not issued, no refund or compensation for damage or loss shall be paid to the holder or any other person in respect of the licence, permit or operating certificate.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "No compensation",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s177",
   "number": "177",
   "text": "If a person fails to pay, within the time required by law, a fine imposed as a result of the person’s conviction for an offence under this Act, then effective immediately as of the date of the failure to pay the fine\n(a) any licence, permit or operating certificate issued to that person is suspended automatically and remains suspended until the earlier of the date on which\n(i) the fine is paid, or\n(ii) the licence, permit or operating certificate expires naturally or is no longer in effect; and\n(b) the person shall not apply for or obtain a licence, permit or operating certificate under this Act until the fine is paid.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Automatic suspension for failure to pay fine",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s178",
   "number": "178",
   "text": "(1) A prosecution for an offence under this Act shall not be commenced after the earlier of\n(a) two years after evidence sufficient to proceed with prosecution of the offence first came to the attention of a conservation officer; or\n(b) three years after the offence was committed.\n(2) Despite subsection 12(1) of the Summary Convictions Act, a ticket may be served within the period for commencing the prosecution of an offence as determined under subsection (1).",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Limitation period",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s179",
   "number": "179",
   "text": "(1) In a prosecution under this Act or in any other proceeding in which proof is required as to\n(a) the issuance, non-issuance, suspension, revocation or cancellation of a licence, permit, operating certificate, outfitting concession or trapping concession;\n(b) whether or not a person is a holder of a licence, permit, operating certificate, outfitting concession or trapping concession;\n(c) the delivery, service, mailing or giving of any notice by the Minister; or\n(d) the designation or authority of a conservation officer or wildlife technician,\na statement signed by the Minister certifying thereto is admissible in evidence as prima facie proof of the facts stated in the statement and is conclusive proof of the authority of the Minister, without proof of the Minister’s appointment or signature.\n(2) In a prosecution or any other proceeding under this Act, a statement signed by the person in charge, or the assistant or a person acting in the place of the person so in charge, of any laboratory or meteorology station operated, maintained, supported or certified by\n(a) the Government of the Yukon;\n(b) the Government of Canada, a province, the United States of America or a state; or\n(c) a university\nis admissible in evidence as prima facie proof of the facts stated in it and is conclusive proof of the authority of the person signing the statement without proof of the person’s appointment or signature.\n(3) The fact that the person charged with the commission of an offence under this Act has the same name as the person referred to in a statement issued under subsection (1) as being the holder of a licence, permit, operating certificate, outfitting concession or trapping concession, is prima facie proof that the person so charged is the holder.",
   "part": "Part 8 — Offences",
   "heading": "Proof of official documents",
