   "part": "Part 11 — Administration",
   "heading": "Administration and enforcement of Act",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s189",
   "number": "189",
   "text": "The Minister may, on behalf of the Government of the Yukon, enter into an agreement with the Government of Canada, the government of a province, a Yukon First Nation or other government, including a municipality, or any other person for the purposes of this Act.",
   "part": "Part 11 — Administration",
   "heading": "Agreements with other governments",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s190",
   "number": "190",
   "text": "(1) The Minister may, in writing, delegate any power, duty or other function of the Minister under a provision of this Act or any agreement entered into pursuant to this Act, to any person including an employee of the Government of the Yukon.\n(2) When the Minister delegates a power, duty or function to a person under this section\n(a) a reference in the provision to the Minister includes the person;\n(b) the delegation may be general or related to a particular case or class of cases and may be for an unlimited time or a specified period of time;\n(c) the delegation may be subject to such terms or conditions as the Minister considers necessary;\n(d) the delegation may be made to the person in the person’s name of office or personal name;\n(e) the person may exercise the power, duty or function in addition to the Minister;\n(f) the person may not subdelegate the power to any other person; and\n(g) the Minister may, by notice in writing, withdraw the delegation.",
   "part": "Part 11 — Administration",
