  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s198",
   "number": "198",
   "text": "(1) In this Part,\n“conservation” means the management of the wildlife populations and habitat to ensure the maintenance of the quality, including the long term optimum productivity of these resources and to ensure the efficient utilization of the available harvest; « protection de la faune »\n“harvesting” includes hunting and trapping; « exploitation de la faune »\n“Herschel Island Territorial Park” means the territorial park established under the Parks Act in accordance with section 12(16) of the Inuvialuit Final Agreement; « parc territorial de l’île Hershel »\n“Hunters and Trappers Committee” means the body established under sections 14(75), 14(76) and 14(77) of the Inuvialuit Final Agreement; « Comité collectif de chasseurs et de trappeurs »\n“Inuvialuit Game Council” means the body created in accordance with sections 14(73) and 14(74) of the Inuvialuit Final Agreement; « Conseil inuvialuit de gestion du gibier »\n“subsistence quota” means the number of animals of a species or population of wildlife on the Yukon North Slope required for subsistence usage and determined in accordance with sections 218 to 225; « quota de subsistance »\n“subsistence usage” means, subject to international conventions, the taking of wildlife by Inuvialuit for their personal use for food and clothing and includes the taking of wildlife for the purpose of trade, barter and, subject to sections 102 and 103, sale among Inuvialuit and trade, barter and sale to any person of the non-edible by-products of wildlife that are incidental to the taking of wildlife by Inuvialuit for their personal use; « utilisation à des fins de subsistance »\n“total allowable harvest” means the number of animals of a species or population of wildlife on the Yukon North Slope which the Minister determines may be harvested in accordance with sections 210 to 217; « limites de prise »\n“Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope)” means the body constituted under section 12(46) of the Inuvialuit Final Agreement. « Conseil consultatif de la gestion de la faune (versant nord) »\n(2) For greater certainty, this Act is subject to the Inuvialuit Final Agreement, and the Inuvialuit Final Agreement prevails over this Act to the extent of any inconsistency or conflict.\n(3) To the extent there is a conflict between any provision of this Part and any other provision of this Act, the provision of this Part prevails to the extent of the conflict.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Interpretation",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s199",
   "number": "199",
   "text": "This Part applies to harvesting of wildlife on the Yukon North Slope by\n(a) Inuvialuit who are harvesting under section 200 or 228; and\n(b) other persons who are allocated harvesting opportunities under sections 229 to 231.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Application",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s200",
   "number": "200",
   "text": "(1) Despite section 6, an Inuvialuk may harvest wildlife throughout the Yukon North Slope, subject to any limitations, restrictions and conditions imposed under this Part.\n(2) Despite subsection (1), when a total allowable harvest has been established for a species or population of wildlife, no person may harvest an animal of that species or population of wildlife unless that person has been allocated an opportunity to harvest that animal under section 226 or under sections 228 to 231.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "General right to harvest",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s201",
   "number": "201",
   "text": "(1) An Inuvialuk may use present and traditional methods of harvesting and may use all equipment reasonably needed to exercise those present and traditional methods of harvesting.\n(2) If required for conservation or for public safety, or to implement international agreements to which the Government of Canada is a party, the Commissioner in Executive Council may, by regulation, limit or restrict the right set out in subsection (1).\n(3) Nothing in this section prevents the Commissioner in Executive Council from limiting or restricting the right set out in subsection (1) pursuant to other legislation respecting conservation or public safety.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Methods of harvest",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s202",
   "number": "202",
   "text": "(1) An Inuvialuk may, without permit, exchange or barter wildlife products on the Yukon North Slope with another Inuvialuk or with a beneficiary of an adjacent land claims agreement.\n(2) Nothing in subsection (1) authorizes the sale of wildlife or any part of the carcass of any wildlife.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Inuvialuit rights to exchange or barter wildlife products",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s203",
   "number": "203",
   "text": "(1) Despite subsection 105(1), but subject to subsections (2), (3) and (4), an Inuvialuk may ship or remove any wildlife or any part of the carcass of any wildlife lawfully harvested under this Part from the Yukon to the Northwest Territories.\n(2) If required for purposes of conservation or public safety, the Commissioner in Executive Council may by regulation prohibit or restrict, or impose conditions upon, the shipping or removal by an Inuvialuk of any wildlife or any part of the carcass of any wildlife from the Yukon.\n(3) An Inuvialuk who ships or removes any wildlife or any part of the carcass of any wildlife from the Yukon to the Northwest Territories under subsection (1) is deemed to have been issued a permit and the permit is deemed to be issued subject to any restriction or condition on the removal of wildlife or any part of a wildlife carcass imposed by regulation made under subsection (2).\n(4) An Inuvialuk who ships or removes any wildlife or any part of the carcass of any wildlife from the Yukon to the Northwest Territories under subsection (1) must comply with any restriction or condition imposed under subsection (2).\n(5) Nothing in this section prevents the Commissioner in Executive Council from limiting or restricting the right set out in subsection (1) pursuant to other legislation respecting conservation or public safety.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Export of Wildlife",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s204",
   "number": "204",
   "text": "Except as provided in section 205, an Inuvialuk is not required to obtain a permit, licence or other authorization to harvest wildlife under this Part.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Exemption from licence requirements",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s205",
   "number": "205",
   "text": "(1) The Commissioner in Executive Council may by regulation require an Inuvialuk to obtain a permit, licence or other authorization to harvest an animal of a species or population of wildlife if\n(a) a total allowable harvest has been established for that species or population; or\n(b) otherwise required for conservation.\n(2) If required for purposes of conservation, the Commissioner in Executive Council may by regulation attach conditions to permits, licences or other authorizations required under subsection (1).\n(3) An Inuvialuk must comply with the conditions of any permit, licence or other authorization required under this section.\n(4) Despite paragraph 192(1)(cc), the Commissioner in Executive Council may not impose a fee or charge for a licence, permit or other authorization required under this Part.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Licences may be required",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s206",
   "number": "206",
   "text": "Despite section 204, an Inuvialuk must, upon request by a conservation officer, show proof of status as an Inuvialuit.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Proof of Inuvialuit status",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s207",
   "number": "207",
   "text": "Despite subsection 8(1), an Inuvialuk may harvest a species of specially protected wildlife if\n(a) the Minister has established a total allowable harvest for that species; and\n(b) Inuvialuit have been allocated an opportunity to harvest animals of that species under section 226 or section 228.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Harvesting of specially protected species",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s208",
   "number": "208",
   "text": "Subsection 8(2) does not apply to an Inuvialuk who has harvested a species of specially protected wildlife in accordance with section 207.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Application of subsection 8(2)",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s209",
   "number": "209",
   "text": "Subsection 8(1) does not apply to a licence which allows the hunting of a species of specially protected wildlife under section 207.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Application of subsection 8(1)",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s210",
   "number": "210",
   "text": "If required for purposes of conservation, the Minister may limit the harvest of a species or population of wildlife on the Yukon North Slope by Inuvialuit and by others, by establishing a total allowable harvest in accordance with sections 211 to 217.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Process for establishing total allowable harvests",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s211",
   "number": "211",
   "text": "(1) If the Minister is of the opinion that conservation requires that a total allowable harvest be established, the Minister may request the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) to recommend a total allowable harvest.\n(2) The Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) may, of its own initiative, recommend to the Minister a total allowable harvest.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Request for recommendation",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s212",
   "number": "212",
   "text": "The Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) must consider conservation and may consider other factors that the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) considers appropriate in determining a total allowable harvest.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Conservation criteria",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s213",
   "number": "213",
   "text": "The Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) must forward its recommended total allowable harvest to the Minister.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Recommendation to Minister",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s214",
   "number": "214",
   "text": "The Minister may accept or reject a total allowable harvest recommended by the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope).",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Consideration of recommendation",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s215",
   "number": "215",
   "text": "If the Minister rejects a total allowable harvest recommended by the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope), the Minister must set out in writing the reasons for the rejection, and must remit the recommendation to the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) with the written reasons and give the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) reasonable time in which to reconsider and make a final recommendation.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Remitted recommendation",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s216",
   "number": "216",
   "text": "(1) When the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) makes a final recommendation to the Minister, the Minister may accept or reject the final recommendation, or may vary or replace the final recommendation.\n(2) If the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) fails to make a final recommendation to the Minister within a reasonable time, the Minister may proceed as though the Wildlife Management Advisory Council’s recommendation under section 213 is the final recommendation of the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope).",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Final recommendation",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s217",
   "number": "217",
   "text": "If the Minister varies or replaces a total allowable harvest recommended by the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope), the Minister must determine the total allowable harvest based only on the requirements of conservation.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Minister’s decision",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s218",
   "number": "218",
   "text": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), if the Minister proposes to implement a total allowable harvest, the Minister must determine the subsistence quota for that species or population of wildlife in accordance with sections 219 to 225.\n(2) Subsection (1) and sections 219 to 225 do not apply if the Minister proposes to establish a total allowable harvest for a fur bearing animal, for polar bear, or for a species or population of wildlife within Herschel Island Territorial Park.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Process for establishing subsistence quotas",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s219",
   "number": "219",
   "text": "(1) If it appears to the Minister that conservation requires that a total allowable harvest be established, the Minister may request the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) to recommend a subsistence quota for that species or population.\n(2) The Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) may, of its own initiative, recommend to the Minister a subsistence quota.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Request for recommendation",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s220",
   "number": "220",
   "text": "In determining a subsistence quota, the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) must take into account\n(a) the food and clothing requirements of the Inuvialuit;\n(b) the usage patterns and levels of harvest of the Inuvialuit;\n(c) the requirements for that particular species or population of wildlife for subsistence usage;\n(d) the availability of wildlife populations to meet subsistence usage requirements including the availability of species from time to time;\n(e) the projections for changes in wildlife populations; and\n(f) other criteria and factors the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) considers appropriate.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Criteria",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s221",
   "number": "221",
   "text": "The Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) must forward its recommended subsistence quota to the Minister.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Recommendation to Minister",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s222",
   "number": "222",
   "text": "The Minister may accept or reject the recommendation of the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope).",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Consideration of recommendation",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s223",
   "number": "223",
   "text": "If the Minister rejects a subsistence quota recommended by the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope), the Minister must set out in writing the Minister’s reasons for rejecting the recommended subsistence quota, and must remit the recommendation to the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) with the written reasons and give the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) reasonable time in which to reconsider and make a final recommendation.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Remitted Recommendation",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s224",
   "number": "224",
   "text": "(1) If the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) makes a final recommendation to the Minister, the Minister may accept or reject the final recommendation, or may vary or replace the final recommendation.\n(2) If the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) fails to make a final recommendation to the Minister within a reasonable time, the Minister may proceed as though the Wildlife Management Advisory Council’s recommendation under section 221 is the final recommendation of the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope).",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Final Recommendation",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s225",
   "number": "225",
   "text": "If the Minister varies or replaces the subsistence quota recommended by the Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope), the Minister must take into account\n(a) the food and clothing requirements of the Inuvialuit;\n(b) the usage patterns and levels of harvest of the Inuvialuit;\n(c) the requirements for that particular species or population of wildlife for subsistence usage;\n(d) the availability of wildlife populations to meet subsistence usage requirements including the availability of species from time to time; and\n(e) the projections for changes in wildlife populations.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Minister’s decision",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s226",
   "number": "226",
   "text": "Subject to section 227, if the Minister establishes a total allowable harvest for a species or population of wildlife, the Minister\n(a) must first allocate to the Inuvialuit Game Council the number of animals equivalent to the lesser of the total allowable harvest or the subsistence quota for that species or population of wildlife; and\n(b) if the total allowable harvest exceeds the subsistence quota for that species or population of wildlife, may allocate any remaining total allowable harvest to other harvesters.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Allocation of preferential harvests",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s227",
   "number": "227",
   "text": "If the Minister establishes a total allowable harvest for\n(a) a fur bearing animal;\n(b) polar bear; or\n(c) a species or population of wildlife in Herschel Island Territorial Park,\nthe Minister must allocate the entire total allowable harvest to the Inuvialuit Game Council.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Allocation of exclusive harvests",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s228",
   "number": "228",
   "text": "If the Minister has allocated all or a portion of a total allowable harvest to the Inuvialuit Game Council under sections 226 or 227, the Inuvialuit may allocate, through the processes set out in the Inuvialuit Final Agreement, the Inuvialuit share among the Inuvialuit.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Suballocation of total allowable harvest to Inuvialuit",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s229",
   "number": "229",
   "text": "(1) If the Minister has allocated a total allowable harvest of polar bear to the Inuvialuit Game Council under section 227, the Inuvialuit may allocate, through the processes set out in the Inuvialuit Final Agreement, an opportunity to harvest a polar bear from the Inuvialuit share to a person who is not Inuvialuit.\n(2) A person to whom the Inuvialuit allocate an opportunity to harvest a polar bear under subsection (1) is subject to all the duties, obligations and prohibitions contained in this Act.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Suballocation of polar bear",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s230",
   "number": "230",
   "text": "(1) If the Minister has allocated a total allowable harvest of a fur bearing animal to the Inuvialuit Game Council under section 227, the Inuvialuit may, with the prior consent of the Minister, allocate, through the processes set out in the Inuvialuit Final Agreement, an opportunity to harvest the fur bearing animal to a person who is not Inuvialuit.\n(2) A person to whom the Inuvialuit allocate an opportunity to harvest a fur bearing animal under subsection (1) is subject to all the duties, obligations and prohibitions contained in this Act.\n(3) The Inuvialuit shall not make a gain or profit from the granting of permission to harvest a fur bearing animal except when the granting of permission is part of a reciprocal arrangement with beneficiaries of an adjacent land claims agreement.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Suballocation of fur bearing animals",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s231",
   "number": "231",
   "text": "(1) If the Minister has allocated a total allowable harvest of a species or population of wildlife, other than a fur bearing animal or polar bear, in Herschel Island Territorial Park to the Inuvialuit Game Council under section 227, the Inuvialuit may allocate, through the processes set out in the Inuvialuit Final Agreement, to a person an opportunity to harvest an animal from that total allowable harvest.\n(2) If under subsection (1) the Inuvialuit allocate an opportunity to harvest to a person who is a beneficiary of an adjacent land claims agreement, that person has, for the purposes of harvesting that wildlife, the same rights and privileges under this Part as an Inuvialuk.\n(3) The Inuvialuit may not allocate an opportunity to harvest wildlife under subsection (1) to a person who is not a beneficiary of an adjacent land claims agreement without the prior consent of the Minister.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Suballocation of wildlife in territorial park",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s232",
   "number": "232",
   "text": "The Inuvialuit Game Council must notify the Minister in writing of the name of each person who is not Inuvialuit and who has been allocated a harvesting opportunity by the Inuvialuit under sections 229, 230, or 231 no later than 30 days after the allocation is made.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Allocations to non-Inuvialuit",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s233",
   "number": "233",
   "text": "(1) If the Minister’s consent is required under sections 230 or 231, the Minister may grant or withhold his or her consent, and the Minister may issue the consent subject to such terms and conditions as the Minister considers appropriate.\n(2) If the Minister has consented to an allocation of wildlife under sections 230 or 231 subject to terms and conditions, no person shall harvest the wildlife except in accordance with the terms and conditions.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Minister’s consent",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s234",
   "number": "234",
   "text": "The Minister may grant any licence, permit or other authorization required to permit the lawful harvest of wildlife by a person to whom the Inuvialuit have allocated a harvesting opportunity under sections 228 to 231.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Grant of authorizations",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s235",
   "number": "235",
   "text": "Nothing in sections 228 to 231 requires the Minister to establish a total allowable harvest.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Minister not obligated",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  },
  {
   "id": "ykwildlife-s236",
   "number": "236",
   "text": "(1) The Wildlife Management Advisory Council (North Slope) may recommend to the Minister that a bylaw of a Hunters and Trappers Committee be adopted as a regulation under this Act.\n(2) The Commissioner in Executive Council may make regulations to implement, in whole or in part, a bylaw of a Hunters and Trappers Committee.\n(3) Nothing in this section imposes a financial obligation on the Minister or the Commissioner in Executive Council, or obligates the Minister or the Commissioner in Executive Council to adopt, implement, or enforce a bylaw of a Hunters and Trappers Committee.",
   "part": "Part 13 — Inuvialuit Final Agreement",
   "heading": "Hunters and Trappers Committee bylaws",
   "instrument": "Wildlife Act (Yukon)"
  }
 ]
}
